# Example requests for the leads API (FR-32), for the VS Code REST Client extension.
# Start the API with `pnpm dev`. The API listens on 127.0.0.1 only (ADR-0003).
# Copy a FAILED lead's id from Prisma Studio (`pnpm db:studio`) until the dashboard (#16) shows it.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:4000
@leadId = paste-a-failed-lead-id-here

### Retry a FAILED lead from its failed step: 200 with the status it starts again from
POST {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/retry

### 409: the same lead again (it is no longer FAILED)
POST {{base}}/leads/{{leadId}}/retry

### 404: unknown lead
POST {{base}}/leads/no-such-lead/retry

### A campaign's lead table: 50 per page, highest score first (FR-30)
@campaignId = paste-a-campaign-id-here
GET {{base}}/campaigns/{{campaignId}}/leads

### Filtered and sorted: HOT leads in DHA scoring 70–100, by review count
GET {{base}}/campaigns/{{campaignId}}/leads?tier=HOT&area=DHA&minScore=70&maxScore=100&sort=reviews&dir=desc

### Page 2
GET {{base}}/campaigns/{{campaignId}}/leads?page=2

### The same filters as a CSV download: exactly the filtered rows
GET {{base}}/campaigns/{{campaignId}}/leads.csv?tier=HOT&area=DHA

### 400: an unknown filter is refused, not ignored
GET {{base}}/campaigns/{{campaignId}}/leads?colour=red
